# The image corpus is a deterministic function of the code and the seed in
# configs/dataset_v1.yaml. Committing ~0.9 GiB of derived JPEGs would make the
# repository permanently expensive to clone and would add nothing the seed does
# not already determine. Everything needed to REGENERATE the images is tracked;
# a curated sample is committed under docs/samples/ so a reviewer can see the
# corpus without building it.
dataset/data/**/images/
dataset/data/**/_crops/

# 21 MB per rebuild, and fully regenerated. manifest.csv (2.3 MB) IS tracked and
# carries the same index in a form you can open in a spreadsheet.
dataset/data/**/manifest.jsonl

# build noise
dataset/logs/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store

# LaTeX build products
paper/*.aux
paper/*.log
paper/*.out
paper/*.toc
paper/*.pdf
!paper/figures/*.pdf
